From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] memory: device-local allocations take their size from the embedder's video memory cap

The embedder registers a table of callbacks (dxvk_proton_set_vram_gate) that
opens one account per device. DxvkMemoryAllocator takes every device-local
allocation's size from it before vkAllocateMemory and gives it back when the
memory is freed, so DXVK, vkd3d and the embedder's other backends on one GPU
share a single cap the guest is told about. Over the cap the allocation is
refused after the empty chunks are returned; with a gate registered nothing
falls back to system memory and DXVK no longer relocates resources between
heaps, because the host driver is never asked to evict for the guest.
---
